message: "If you use this work, please cite the accompanying conceptual synthesis note."
title: "Constraint Geometry and Domain Physics: A Two-Layer Architecture for Binary Partition Diagnostics"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "De Jesús"
    given-names: "Elias"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0190-9143"
abstract: >-
  A conceptual synthesis note on the division of labor between binary-partition
  constraint geometry and domain physics. Constraint geometry supplies a
  conserved partition, intrinsic coordinates, response measures, and exactly
  located relational landmarks; domain physics supplies the sectors, the
  normalization, the embedding of physical variables into the partition, the
  dynamics, and any empirical meaning. A physical diagnostic emerges only where
  the two layers intersect under an independently justified map. The note gives
  a five-step protocol, a set of safeguards, an explicit epistemic tiering, and
  worked readings in perturbative general relativity, flat Lambda-CDM,
  effective potentials, and Newtonian two-body mechanics.
keywords:
  - constraint geometry
  - binary partition
  - Thales altitude
  - domain embedding
  - intrinsic relational landmark
  - compactness diagnostic
  - perturbative general relativity
  - epistemic tiering
